# Figure colors

Set the defaults with the script. Do not edit the color lines by hand.

```bash
scripts/set-colors.py <<'EOF'
Skin: new Color(1f, 1f, 1f)
Joints: new Color(0.6f, 0.8f, 0.98f)
Ground: new Color(0.48f, 0.54f, 0.58f, 0.92f)
Background: new Color(0.19f, 0.19f, 0.19f)
Main light: 1.3f
Fill light: new Color(0.92f, 0.95f, 1f)
EOF
```

- Pass the user's block as-is. Any subset of lines works.
- With no input piped in, the script reads the clipboard. The user can press Copy all in the Colors menu and run `scripts/set-colors.py`.
- The Colors menu drops saved picks when the defaults change, so the new defaults show on the next Play.
- Then tell the user to stop Play and press Play again. Do not re-record the videos unless the user explicitly asks.
